## Development Workflow

### Branch Rules

- Always create a feature branch before starting work
- Branch naming: `<prefix>-<task-id>/<short-description>`
- Never commit directly to main/master
- One task per branch — keep changes atomic

### Commit Rules

- Atomic commits: one logical change per commit
- Conventional commit messages: `type(scope): description`
- Types: feat, fix, chore, refactor, test, docs, style, perf, ci
- Always run tests before committing
- Always run linting before committing

### Task Workflow

1. Check for an assigned/in-progress task before starting new work
2. Set task to in-progress when starting
3. Create a feature branch from main
4. Implement the task (test-first when possible)
5. Verify all tests pass and lint is clean
6. Commit with a descriptive message referencing the task ID
7. Close the task when complete
8. Open a PR if the project uses pull requests

## Agent Instructions

These instructions apply to any AI coding agent working on this project:

- Read this file and the project's main config file before making changes
- Follow the coding conventions defined above
- Run tests after every significant change
- Do not modify files outside the scope of the current task
- Check for existing patterns before introducing new ones
- Prefer editing existing files over creating new ones
- Do not add dependencies without justification
- When in doubt, ask — do not guess at requirements

